                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "2048 is an addictive puzzle game where you pair up identical numbers.\nTiles with the number 2 gets dropped in a 4x4 grid, you'll have to pair those to make them 4,8,16,32,64,128 and so on.\nYou keep playing till you reach the 2048 tile or until the grid is filled with tiles and it's game over.\n\nIn this version the numbers got replaced for tiles with historical monuments.\nBy pairing two of the same, a new one appears and as you unlock more historical monuments, you slowly travel through the evolution of mankind. \n\nThe game runs smoothly, the graphics look great, and the color scheme used make the game pleasant to look at.\nThe game is both relaxing and frustrating at the same time, and I'm glad the developer implemented an undo option.\nHowever, the waiting time after using the undo option doesn't make much sense to me...\nThere is a lot of detail in the tiles that I wish I could look at up close.\nIt would also be nice if you could change the angle of the board.\n\nApart from a few displeasing factors, my overall experience with the game is great, and I specially recommend it to those that enjoy 2048 games.",
